# ---
# title: ladder integrity — population
# description: >
#   Every claim the ladder-integrity gate could judge: a normative statement
#   carrying a rung. The gate's own WHERE cannot answer this, because its
#   judgement lives in FILTER NOT EXISTS inside the pattern — so on a healthy
#   corpus it matches nothing and a derived count reads zero for a gate that just
#   examined the whole corpus.
# severity: error
# ---
# ⛔ AUTHORED, AND THAT IS THE RISK. Nothing mechanically proves this pattern is
# the gate's candidate set. If it drifts wider than the gate, a gate that
# examined nothing wears a large number and reads as thorough — strictly worse
# than silence. Two cheap guards exist and neither is a proof: gate_cli refuses a
# population smaller than the violation count, and where the gate has a HAVING it
# derives the count independently and reports disagreement. Review this file and
# its gate together or not at all.
PREFIX rfc: <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/rfc#>
PREFIX au:  <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/authoring#>
SELECT ?claim
WHERE {
  ?claim a rfc:NormativeStatement ; au:rung ?rung .
}
